# Release notes: v0.3.6

File: tui/docs/release_0_3_6.oot

The work screen you type with. Version 0.3.6 is a hardening release:
no new big features, but safer paths, cleaner exits, and a fresher
build chain. Tagged `v0.3.6`.

## What changed since v0.3.3

- Portable install paths. The screen no longer assumes fixed home
  folder spots. It follows your setup instead.
- No hardcoded user paths. A guard refuses paths that try to escape
  the workspace. Nasty `..` tricks fail closed.
- Clean exits for batch and pipe runs. Waiting output is flushed
  before quit, so scripted runs lose nothing.
- Build chain v0.11.15 with tiered runtime libraries. The 138-case
  end-to-end gate runs in the build with portable paths.

## What stayed the same

- The three-zone layout: prompt dock on top, thought canvas in the
  middle, status dashboard at the bottom.
- The 138-case end-to-end suite under the double-run rule: run it
  twice, both runs must agree.
- Themes, slash commands, and the editor/AI helper connections.

## Upgrade

Re-run the setup script. Your settings carry over. If the screen
misbehaves after upgrade, quit fully and start it once more before
reporting trouble.
